	<!--
		Muragan the Loyal (800435). Retail route Path_IDTiamat_Murugan_1, from the client's own
		Map/Worlds/idtiamat_1/world_N_WayPoint_1.xml, extracted with
		tools/client-extract/extract_client_waypoints.py. The world resolves to this map through the
		cName on world_maps.xml.

		The first point is his spawn (930.91, 1316.27, 401) to within half a metre, and the sixth is the
		door he walks to. Points seven to eleven walk him back the way he came: the client authors this
		as an out-and-back, and retail's IDTiamat_Murugan1 despawns him at the sixth, so the return half
		is never used by him. It is kept because it is the route as shipped, and trimming data to match
		one consumer's use of it is how the next reader gets misled.

		NOT YET BOUND TO A SPAWN. Giving 800435 a walker_id here would set him patrolling from the moment
		the instance opens, and retail has him stand still until a player comes within fifteen metres.
		Wiring it needs MuraganAI to start the walk itself, which is the next piece of work; see
		docs/retail-ai-fidelity.md.
	-->
